   "sentenceId": 14,
   "he": "רַבָּן שִׁמְעוֹן בֶּן גַּמְלִיאֵל אוֹמֵר: שֶׁל נַחְתּוֹמִים וְשֶׁל צַבָּעִין שָׁלֹשׁ שָׁנִים. תָּנָא: מִפְּנֵי שֶׁהֶקֵּיפָן מְרוּבֶּה.",
   "en": "§ The mishna teaches: «Rabban Shimon ben Gamliel says:» For «a baker’s shop or a dyer’s shop,» one must give «three years’» notice. «It was taught» in a baraita (Tosefta 8:27): The need for this unusually long period of notice is «due to» the fact «that» the length of the «credit» extended by these businesses to their customers «is extensive.» They must be provided with enough time to collect their debts before being forced to relocate."
  }
